SOMA Retargeter — retargeter-suite fork
========================================

This repository is a fork of NVIDIA's SOMA Retargeter
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/soma-retargeter, Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE).
Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES for the upstream code and
bundled assets; the upstream LICENSE, SPDX headers and licenses/ directory are
kept unchanged. Third-party robot descriptions keep their own licences:
Unitree, Booster and AgiBot assets as listed in LICENSE and licenses/; the
Unitree H1-2 and R1 and Booster T1/K1 descriptions under assets/robots/ are
redistributed under the licences stated in their source repositories
(Unitree BSD-3-Clause, Booster Robotics Apache-2.0); the ROBOTIS AI Sapiens
description is pulled in as a git submodule (third_party/ai_sapiens) under
its own licence.

Modifications relative to upstream v0.2.0 (branch retargeter-suite,
github.com/nicolejrkim/soma-retargeter):

* soma_retargeter/legacy/ — the v0.1.0-lineage pipeline (NewtonPipeline,
  FeetStabilizer, per-joint-scale HumanToRobotScaler, RobotSpec registry,
  CSV writers) kept beside the v0.2.0 SomaRetargetingPipeline so that the
  recipes published with this fork reproduce bit for bit. Fork additions
  inside it: a robot registry (RobotSpec), Unitree H1-2 (27 dof), Unitree R1
  (24 dof), Booster T1 (23 dof and 29 dof rigs), Booster K1 (22 dof) and
  ROBOTIS AI Sapiens targets; scaler position-offset modes and per-joint
  overrides; temporal joint reference, neutral reference and limb reach
  projection objectives; stance foot lock; pelvis floor; AI Sapiens staged
  solver and arm objectives (merged from ROBOTIS-GIT/soma-retargeter).
* soma_retargeter/configs/<robot>/ — the fork's retargeter, scaler and feet
  stabilizer configs for the legacy pipeline (unitree_g1 configs are the
  unchanged v0.1.0 files).
* assets/robots/ — MJCF descriptions and meshes for the fork's robots.
* app/bvh_to_csv_converter.py — upstream converter plus a dispatch to
  app/bvh_to_csv_converter_legacy.py (the fork's converter) selected by the
  converter config ("pipeline", retargeter-config format or target name).
* pyproject.toml — pinned to newton 1.0.0 / warp-lang 1.12.0 instead of
  upstream's newton 1.3.0 / warp-lang >= 1.14 (Newton 1.3.0 changes the IK
  solution by up to ~1 deg on the fork's recipes); mujoco and GitPython added.
* tools/ — AI Sapiens MJCF generation and comparison helpers.
